        obo:IAO_0000115  "Does the ontology use valid URIs to encode some metadata values? This metric corresponds to the O'FAIRe question I3Q3, which assesses FAIR principle I3. Its raw value is the number of credits obtained in the question, measured on an ordinal scale with the following levels: 0 (The ontology does not use URIs to encode metadata values); 1 (The ontology provides at least 1 metadata value encoded as URI); 2 (The ontology provides at least 2 metadata values encoded as URIs); 3 (The ontology provides at least 3 metadata values encoded as URIs); 4 (The ontology provides at least 4 metadata values encoded as URIs); 5 (The ontology provides at least 5 metadata values encoded as URIs); 6 (The ontology provides at least 6 metadata values encoded as URIs); 7 (The ontology provides at least 7 metadata values encoded as URIs)."@en ;
